(go/const ^{:val 509} outbufMode 0775)









































(go/type OutBuf "OutBuf is a buffered file writer.\n\nIt is similar to the Writer in cmd/internal/bio with a few small differences.\n\nFirst, it tracks the output architecture and uses it to provide\nendian helpers.\n\nSecond, it provides a very cheap offset counter that doesn't require\nany system calls to read the value.\n\nThird, it also mmaps the output file (if available). The intended usage is:\n  - Mmap the output file\n  - Write the content\n  - possibly apply any edits in the output buffer\n  - possibly write more content to the file. These writes take place in a heap\n    backed buffer that will get synced to disk.\n  - Munmap the output file\n\nAnd finally, it provides a mechanism by which you can multithread the\nwriting of output files. This mechanism is accomplished by copying a OutBuf,\nand using it in the thread/goroutine.\n\nParallel OutBuf is intended to be used like:\n\n\tfunc write(out *OutBuf) {\n\t  var wg sync.WaitGroup\n\t  for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {\n\t    wg.Add(1)\n\t    view, err := out.View(start[i])\n\t    if err != nil {\n\t       // handle output\n\t       continue\n\t    }\n\t    go func(out *OutBuf, i int) {\n\t      // do output\n\t      wg.Done()\n\t    }(view, i)\n\t  }\n\t  wg.Wait()\n\t}\n" (struct
    ^{:line 63 :tag (* sys/Arch)} arch
    ^{:line 64 :tag int64} off

    ^{:line 66 :tag (slice byte)} buf ; backing store of mmap'd output file
    ^{:line 67 :tag (slice byte)} heap ; backing store for non-mmapped data

    ^{:line 69 :tag string} name
    ^{:line 70 :tag (* os/File)} f
    ^{:line 71 :tag (array 8 byte)} encbuf ; temp buffer used by WriteN methods
    ^{:line 72 :tag bool} isView)) ; true if created from View()


